{
 "_about": "Copied from HusbandOutWorld's content/i18n/ja/glossary.json, so the campaign, the novel and the game spell every name the same way. When a spelling changes, change it there and copy it here (or the other way round). \"campaign\" adds this campaign's own names and game words; \"dnd5e\" lists the D&D 5e rules terms of this language's published edition, so players recognise them from their books. Add a new name the first time you translate it.",
 "rule": "Story names in katakana, by sound. This covers coined world terms too: creatures, plants, items, nari gels, factions, guilds, places, ranks and coins (Wood People = ウッドピープル, Fost Stone = フォストストーン, Sapphire = サファイア, balls = ボール). Multi-word names join with ・. Real people (Deovandski, Mitsukiven, Feiourm) and pets named in the afterwords (Peeta, Fluffy, Maddog) stay in Latin letters. Plain words are translated.",
